\title{The Addition Rule}
\date{2026-04-28T23:44:00Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Principle}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Suppose choosing something means \em{either} making one choice in #{c_1} ways \em{or} making another choice in #{c_2} ways, and the choices do not overlap at all. Then the total number of choices is #{c_1 + c_2}.}
\p{In other words, when #{A} and #{B} are disjoint, ##{|A \cup B| = |A| +
    |B|.}}

